import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for FC Mobile Tools by TanzimFC.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / PRIVACY</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: October 9, 2026</p>

    <section><h2>1. Who operates this site</h2><p>FC Mobile Tools ("FCMOBILETOOLS", "we", "us", or "our") is an independent fan project operated by TanzimFC. This policy explains how information may be processed when you visit or use our website, tools, articles, creator workspace, and related services.</p></section>

    <section><h2>2. Public browsing and FCMobiletools accounts</h2><p>Most public tools and information pages can be used without an account. If you register for an FCMobiletools account, we may process your email address and authentication identifiers, username, display name, avatar URL, account status, profile settings, XP and streak progress, achievements, task and quest history, Token ledger records, survey responses, and security or moderation records needed to run the service.</p><p>Some account features also record qualifying interactions so the server can verify activity, prevent duplicate claims, and calculate progress. Depending on the feature, those records may include an article or page identifier, a tool used, reading progress or time spent, a captain-tracker selection, a survey answer, a timestamp, and the status of a quest or reward claim. These records are distinct from general website analytics and are associated with the account using the feature.</p><p>Public profile pages, leaderboards, and tournament features may display a username, avatar, selected public profile fields, public progress, rankings, or competition information. We limit public profile output to fields intended for public display; email addresses, authentication credentials, private security records, and reward-delivery details are not part of the public profile. Some account-only features, including quests and surveys, require a confirmed email address.</p></section>

    <section><h2>3. Creator and private workspace data</h2><p>The private creator/admin system is separate from ordinary community accounts and public browsing. Creator accounts may contain a username, display name, password credential data, profile information, website or avatar information, article drafts, revisions, review notes, publishing records, and related editorial metadata. Passwords are stored as password hashes rather than as readable passwords.</p><p>Administrative authentication also uses security session cookies. These private systems are intended for authorized personnel and contributors, not ordinary public visitors.</p></section>

    <section><h2>4. Information processed automatically</h2><p>Like most websites, our hosting and security infrastructure may process technical request information needed to deliver pages, APIs, images, and security functions. Depending on the service involved, this can include IP address, browser or device characteristics, request information, timestamps, and diagnostic information. We do not use this section to promise that a particular infrastructure provider retains or deletes logs on a specific schedule; provider-specific practices are governed by their own terms and policies.</p></section>

    <section><h2>5. Analytics</h2><p>FCMOBILETOOLS uses Google Analytics to understand website usage, such as which pages are viewed and general traffic or technical patterns. The shared site layout sets Google's non-essential storage signals to denied by default and updates them when a visitor saves an analytics choice through the privacy controls. Google may still receive limited consent-related or cookieless requests under its own implementation; a denied storage signal should not be read as a promise that no request is sent or no information is processed. Analytics information is used to assess site performance and improve tools and content.</p></section>

    <section id="privacy-choices"><h2>6. Cookies, consent, and browser storage</h2><p>The site uses cookies and similar technologies for privacy preferences, analytics, advertising, security, and signed-in or private workspaces. The shared privacy-controls component can store a <code>fcmobiletools_consent</code> cookie recording the selected analytics and advertising choices, a consent version, and a timestamp. Its configured lifetime is approximately 180 days. The shared layout sends relevant choices to Google's consent signals. This does not necessarily block every third-party script or request before a choice is made, and older standalone pages or embedded services may use separate integrations.</p><p>Public tools and older or legacy features may store preferences, predictions, progress, quiz state, settings, or other feature data in local storage. The account sign-in flow may also use browser storage to maintain authentication state. Clearing browser data may remove saved tool progress or sign you out. You can manage browser storage and cookies through your browser and, where available, reopen the site's controls through the Privacy Choices link. See our <a href="/legal/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.</p></section>

    <section><h2>7. Third-party services</h2><p>The site uses or links to third-party services that may process information when your browser connects to them. These include Google Analytics and Google advertising services, Google Fonts, Supabase services used for account authentication and related data, Cloudflare hosting, Workers and D1 infrastructure, Cloudinary for media delivery, and external platforms such as YouTube, Discord, X, and EA services. Embedded videos, external links, and hosted images can cause your browser to contact the relevant provider directly. Each provider's own terms and privacy policy apply to its processing.</p></section>

    <section><h2>8. Images and content delivery</h2><p>Site images may be delivered from Cloudinary or other external hosts. Public article and event content can therefore cause your browser to request an image or other resource from a third-party domain. The presence of a third-party resource does not mean that we control that provider's privacy practices.</p></section>

    <section><h2>9. How information is used</h2><p>Information may be used to operate and secure the site, authenticate accounts and authorized staff, maintain profiles and editorial content, respond to requests, review submissions, prevent abuse, investigate technical problems, understand aggregate website use, and meet applicable obligations. Account activity records can be used to verify eligible quest progress, apply anti-duplication or rate limits, administer survey rewards, record community tracker votes, maintain leaderboards, and link participants to tournament records where that feature is used. Reading or interaction records are not a guarantee that a reward will be issued; eligibility is checked by the relevant feature's rules.</p></section>

    <section><h2>10. Data retention</h2><p>Retention depends on the type of information, the feature involved, and why the record is needed. Local browser data can remain until you clear it or it expires. Account, quest, survey, voting, leaderboard, tournament, reward, creator, and editorial records may be kept while needed to provide the feature, preserve accurate balances or results, investigate misuse, resolve disputes, maintain security, or comply with applicable obligations. Infrastructure providers may apply their own log-retention periods. We do not promise indefinite storage or deletion on a fixed timetable.</p></section>

    <section><h2>11. Security</h2><p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to the service, including authenticated private workspaces, password hashing for creator credentials, signed sessions, and access controls. No website, cloud service, database, or transmission over the internet can be guaranteed completely secure. You should use strong, unique credentials and should not share private workspace passwords.</p></section>

    <section><h2>12. Children</h2><p>The public site is a general FC Mobile fan resource. We do not knowingly seek to collect personal information from children through the public site. If you believe personal information was submitted to us by a child and requires attention, contact us through the channels listed on the <a href="/legal/contact">Contact</a> page.</p></section>

    <section><h2>13. International processing</h2><p>Because our hosting, analytics, media, and other service providers may operate in different countries, information may be processed outside the country where you live. The safeguards and legal mechanisms applicable to a particular provider depend on that provider and the circumstances of the processing.</p></section>

    <section><h2>14. External websites</h2><p>Links to EA, YouTube, Discord, X, and other websites take you outside FCMOBILETOOLS. We do not control those services and are not responsible for their privacy practices, security, content, or availability.</p></section>

    <section><h2>15. Your choices and requests</h2><p>You can stop using the site, clear browser data, manage cookies, adjust the privacy choices available to you, and decline to provide optional information. You may also request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information you directly provided to FCMOBILETOOLS by contacting us through the official channels on the <a href="/legal/contact">Contact</a> page. We may need to verify the request and may retain limited records where permitted or required for security, fraud prevention, rewards accounting, disputes, or legal obligations. The outcome and timing depend on the information and applicable requirements.</p></section>

    <section><h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may revise this policy when the site, infrastructure, services, or applicable requirements change. The "Last updated" date identifies the current version. Where appropriate, material changes may also be communicated through the site or relevant community channels.</p></section>

    <section><h2>17. Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions or requests, use the official channels listed on the <a href="/legal/contact">Contact</a> page. Please do not send passwords, authentication tokens, payment details, or other unnecessary sensitive information through community messages.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
